A(('p', '13.2 Neighboring parables. The Wedding Banquet, the Faithful and Unfaithful Servant, the Talents and the Sheep and the Goats are each read in their own study of the Parable Studies. This parable makes no use of their meanings, and they make none of this one.'))
A(('p', '13.3 Final Synthesis. Jesus likens the kingdom of heaven to ten virgins who took their lamps and went forth to meet the bridegroom. Five were wise and took oil in their vessels; five were foolish and took none. The bridegroom tarried and they all slept. At midnight a cry was made, the foolish went to buy, the bridegroom came, the ready went in with him to the marriage, and the door was shut. The other virgins knocked and were answered, “I know you not.” Jesus ends with “Watch therefore, for ye know neither the day nor the hour wherein the Son of man cometh.” He gives no explanation and names none of the parts. The comparison says that readiness is prepared beforehand, that the hour of the coming is not known, and that a shut door is not reopened by knocking.'))
